  "worked_solution": "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{H}^{\u2032}(t)\u2248\\frac{H(t+h)-H(t)}{h},\n$$\n\nat the time $t=9$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}^{\u2032}(9) & \u2248\\frac{H(9+2)-H(9)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{H(11)-H(9)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-80}{2} \\\\  & =-40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after $9$ minutes, the rate of change of the height is $-40$ meters per minute.",
